-- statement:
--   Primitive (b), split: all `W` streams of the cyclic row split, concatenated on stack `0` (arguments `1, W, P * L, vol rest` on stacks `1 … 4`), cost `O(W · V)`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KILRow`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KIL.rowSplit_spec (t : IState HS) (xs : List ℤ) (P W L : ℕ) (rest : Shape) (Bb : ℕ)
--       (R L1 L2 L3 L4 : List Item)
--       (hlen : xs.length = AModel.vol (P :: W * L :: rest)) (hb : Bnd Bb xs)
--       (hB1 : 1 ≤ AModel.vol rest) (hPL : 1 ≤ P * L) (hW : 1 ≤ W)
--       (hV : zsz ((1 * (W * (P * L * AModel.vol rest)) : ℕ) : ℤ) ≤ Bb)
--       (h0 : t.G 0 = ints xs ++ R) (h1 : t.G 1 = .int ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ) :: L1)
--       (h2 : t.G 2 = .int (W : ℤ) :: L2) (h3 : t.G 3 = .int ((P * L : ℕ) : ℤ) :: L3)
--       (h4 : t.G 4 = .int (AModel.vol rest : ℤ) :: L4) :
--       bwdP.ok t ∧ bwdP.run t = t.upd 0 (ints ((List.finRange W).flatMap
--           (fun w => rowSplit P W L rest w 0 xs)) ++ R) ∧
--         bwdP.cost t ≤ cMove 1 W (P * L) (AModel.vol rest) Bb
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *Primitive (b): cyclic row split / merge (`rowSplit`, `rowMerge` of `AModelNet`)*: The `W` streams are stored one after the other (stream `0` on top).  On `P :: (W * L) :: rest`
--   with `B = vol rest`, the concatenation of the streams is the move of the row-class digit `w`
--   (`r = W g + w`) to the front: `bwdP` with parameters `1, W, P * L, B` splits, `fwdP` merges, both
--   in `O(W · V)` item moves.
